    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.05), our two strongest plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Yesavage, where a plus-11% SP skill adjustment and a 14% platoon edge solidify his position as a core start. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** is poised to exploit a high-ceiling outing against Patrick Sandoval, with our optimizer favoring his projected leadoff spot and a 10% efficiency bump from park factors. **Kyle Tucker** (59.68) and **Jackson Merrill** (59.43) remain reliable anchors; while **Kyle Tucker** faces a respectable Emerson Hancock, his raw talent and expected order positioning keep him comfortably in the upper echelon of today\u2019s recommendations.\n\nTactical decision-making focused heavily on mitigating the impact of elite arms like Skubal. **Gunnar Henderson** (45.90) serves as a necessary exception, as his base production remains too valuable to bench despite a significant 19% downgrade due to Skubal's elite SP skill. Our most difficult omission was **Dominic Smith** (45.18), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Andy Pages** (58.00). While **Dominic Smith** is a capable utility option, the optimizer favored **Andy Pages**\u2014whose slow-delivery matchup against Emerson Hancock provides a sneaky boost for potential stolen base opportunities\u2014and the situational reliability of our core infielders. We are monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** (52.66) and **Drake Baldwin** (54.11) closely, as both face a 45% rain risk; should weather force a postponement, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though **Coby Mayo** (44.22) and **Heliot Ramos** (42.66) currently trail our starters in daily efficiency.",
